\ A definition made inside a called quotation is exempt from the collision guards, because the
\ quotation body runs in a transient lexical frame and the binding pops with it.
\
\ The helper shadows a prelude word and is never called. Calling it would fail the freeze as a
\ nested definition, which would turn this runtime-legality pin into a build failure.

[ nip: ( -- y ) [ 42 ] ; ] call

"after" print-line
